# Secrets and machine-local overrides. Copy to `.env`. NEVER commit `.env`.
#
# Its job is now narrow: this file holds SECRETS. Structure and choices - which
# providers, capture device, segmentation, delivery - live in `livesubs.yaml`.
# See `livesubs.yaml.example` and docs/12-configuration.md.
#
# The recommended way to fill this in is:
#   livesubs --set-key deepgram        # hidden prompt, writes here with 0600
#   livesubs --set-key deepseek
#   livesubs --keys                    # show status, masked, with the source
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   1. a real environment variable   export DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=...
#   2. ./.env                        (this file)
#   3. ~/.config/livesubs/.env
#   4. livesubs.yaml
#   5. built-in defaults
#
# So exporting a value is how you override anything for a single session without
# touching disk, and any LIVESUBS_* setting can be overridden the same way:
#   export LIVESUBS_PORT=9000

# --- Credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
# One of the ASR keys and one of the MT keys must be set for the live pipeline to
# start. Everything a provider needs besides its key (endpoint, model, mode)
# lives in the provider registry and can be retuned in livesubs.yaml.
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Planned provider, not integrated yet: storing a key does not make it work, and
# it does not satisfy the MT requirement. See docs/05-providers.md.
DEEPL_API_KEY=
